Do not invent a generic Exotel/LiveKit integration.

Before implementation:

- Read current official Exotel voice, streaming, SIP, webhook, status callback, recording, and call-detail documentation.
- Confirm which capability the configured Exotel account supports.
- Determine the officially supported audio transport: SIP, media streaming, WebSocket, or another documented mechanism.
- Confirm codecs, sample rates, call initiation API, callback format, callback authentication, call IDs, duration fields, rate limits, regional requirements, and disconnect controls.
- Document which integration path is implemented and why.
- If account enablement is required, complete the adapter, validation, mocks, and documentation, then report the exact account-side capability that must be enabled.
- Never claim PSTN calling works until a real controlled phone call has been completed.

