Design requirements:

- Strong, modern visual hierarchy.
- Excellent desktop and mobile responsiveness.
- Accessible keyboard navigation, focus states, labels, contrast, and reduced-motion support.
- Skeletons, empty states, errors, retry states, confirmations, and success feedback.
- Avoid hydration differences and browser-only values during server rendering.
- Use subtle motion and depth.
- Use tasteful 3D or layered visual elements only where they improve the landing page or product comprehension.
- Do not add heavy WebGL, large assets, or distracting effects to operational dashboard pages.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Optimize Core Web Vitals and bundle size.
- Keep operational pages clean and fast.

Do not show mocked values as real business data.

## Milestone 3: Finish agents and browser voice testing

- Complete agent details and versioning or immutable configuration snapshots.
- Validate supported Sarvam voices and languages using current official documentation.
- Allow safe model settings only through approved server-side configuration.
- Show worker/provider readiness.
- Show live connection, listening, thinking, speaking, interrupted, reconnecting, failed, and ended states.
- Make transcript updates stable without duplicates.
- Add session timing diagnostics.
- Add download/export of safe diagnostic events without credentials.
- Test two agents with different instructions.
- Test Telugu, Hindi, Indian English, and code-switching.
- Test rapid start/end, navigation, reconnect, microphone failure, worker failure, provider failure, and cancellation races.
